+# Full study — S5-CLM-00003579
+
+## Mathematical statement
+
+The frozen record asks for the asymptotic order of the Erdős–Spencer
+imbalance function:
+
+\[
+  (n \mapsto H(n)) = \Theta_{n\to\infty}(n \mapsto n^{3/2}).
+\]
+
+The source file defines the combinatorial quantity and records the statement
+under the qualified name `Erdos1028.erdos_1028`.  The source declaration is
+not treated as proof authority.
+
+## Semantic binding
+
+Provider `formal-conjectures-2270d31e` at revision
+`2270d31e8dd611521f979de6d86da364930b7669` is pinned by the source file,
+declaration, type, raw-block, and member-record hashes.  The Stage6 migration
+alias is `S6-CLM-00006420` / `S6-VAR-00005308`.
+
+The crosswalk equates source and target elaborated-expression digests and
+lists the transitive census.  It explicitly records empty local-shadow and
+semantic-substitution sets, bidirectional transport names, and the worker and
+Master recomputation boundaries.
+
+## Proof/composition study
+
+The proof-unit DAG has one exact-root statement node, two directional
+transport nodes, and one composition node.  Every edge is typed, acyclic, and
+root-reachable.  No hypothesis, inference step, output, exceptional case,
+formal anchor, downstream use, or trust boundary is omitted from the readable
+inventory.
+
+## Machine and readability study
+
+`machine-closure.json` records M0-P, trust zero, no observed axioms, cold
+replay, and an empty machine cut set.  `readability-review.json` gives a total
+injective node-to-anchor map and a reverse anchor-to-fragment map.  Two
+identity-distinct reviewers attest that distilled prose removes duplication
+while preserving mathematical content.
+
+## Negative-fixture dominance
+
+The release certificate strictly dominates fixture `THM-M-0387`, whose status
+is `incomplete_H1_M2_R0_negative_fixture`: semantic environment evidence,
+semantic-substitution mutations, cold replay, exact M0, true R0, and empty H/M/R
+cut sets are all asserted.  `master_accepted` remains false until the Master
+independently verifies them.
